135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 109 0 R
/E (This project develops a machine learning-based system to detect fraudulent credit card transactions using real-world transaction data. Utilizing the Kaggle Credit Card Fraud Dataset with 284,807 transactions, the system employs Logistic Regression and Decision Tree classifiers, along with undersampling and SMOTE oversampling techniques to address severe class imbalance. The model assists financial institutions in accurately identifying fraudulent activity, achieving up to 93.8% accuracy with high precision and recall, thereby reducing financial losses. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
