255 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (This project successfully engineered and evaluated a machine learning classification system designed to detect credit card fraud with high precision and recall. By systematically addressing the challenge of extreme class imbalance through undersampling and SMOTE strategies, and evaluating Logistic Regression and Decision Tree classifiers, the system demonstrated strong detection performance across all tested conditions. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
256 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (The Decision Tree model with undersampled data achieved the best F1 Score of 0.940, with Precision of 96.9% and Recall of 91.3%. Beyond pure predictive power, the project demonstrated that raw accuracy is a misleading metric for imbalanced datasets, and that balanced sampling is essential to build truly effective fraud detectors. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
257 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (Ultimately, this project highlights the immense potential of Machine Learning not as a replacement for fraud analysts, but as a force-multiplying tool. By automating the screening of millions of daily transactions, reducing false positives, and providing interpretable fraud signals, ML-enhanced systems represent the future of financial security. AI-augmented fraud detection will be instrumental in reducing losses, protecting cardholders, and maintaining trust in digital payment ecosystems globally. )
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
